Felice aus Salum wrote:

> I only started to play nethack a week ago and have some questions on
> what and how I can do:

Welcome!

> 1.) Is it possible to only sip at a potion before swallowing the
> whole? I'm thinking of testing for poison for example or already
> getting this typical mesage, that lets me guess, what this potion is.
> If not so: Is there a way of identifying potion without scroll of
> identify without swallowing or throwing at monsters?

No. A potion only has effects (good or bad) after you swallow it whole.

Some potions can be identified by dipping other things in them. For
example, dipping something in a potion of polymorph will change it into
something else, dipping arrows in a potion of sickness will poison them,
etc. And a clear potion does not need to be identified: it's always
water (or holy or unholy water).

> 2.) Is it possible to mix potions? Can it have funny effects if I
> swallow to many different potions one after the other? If this is the
> case I'd rather like to test these effects outside my body, than
> inside:-)

Effects rarely influence earlier potion effects, apart from, for
example, a potion of healing curing the effects of a potion of
blindness.

And yes, you can mix potions. I'm not giving any details, you might want
to experiment. To mix, dip potion A in potion B. Some combinations give
fixed effects, some are random. For example: dipping ANYTHING in holy
water will bless it.

